{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123341","id":4486999767,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABC3Iu1w","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123341","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123341.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123341.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123341","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123341/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123341/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123341/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/dfac7c8e9fff651e63364bdc736f6de11437811b","number":123341,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"LightmapGI: Address seam leaks in surface sampling and ray traversal","user":{"login":"tinomarques","id":59707674,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU5NzA3Njc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/59707674?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques","html_url":"https://github.com/tinomarques","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tinomarques/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Addresses the light leaks reported in #117468 using its reproduction project.\r\n\r\nMy first commit used limited AI assistance, but every subsequent commit used AI much more heavily as my understanding of the other three files was more limited. This involved GPT-6 Astra running in an investigate-code-test loop for about 2 hours under my guidance and monitoring.\r\n\r\nI understand that the later commits may not be acceptable under the contribution guidelines, but I hope the findings and reproduction results can still be useful to other contributors, even if the full implementation cannot be accepted.\r\n\r\n| Image set | Before | After |\r\n|---|---|---|\r\n| Outside | <img width=\"1280\" height=\"1200\" alt=\"before-1\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/18744a2f-c18c-4cb2-b1bc-1891a9b468b9\" /> | <img width=\"1280\" height=\"1200\" alt=\"after-1\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d1ed1166-77be-41fb-9cbc-2ff98ead2a07\" /> |\r\n| Original mesh | <img width=\"1000\" height=\"800\" alt=\"before-2\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/13c0c9fe-17fc-4208-81dc-f492464a0334\" /> | <img width=\"1000\" height=\"800\" alt=\"after-2\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9c99b4a6-9f44-43c2-a3cc-0bce44c8dcea\" /> |\r\n| Smooth mesh | <img width=\"1000\" height=\"800\" alt=\"before-3\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2bcdb461-806c-4b3b-9d14-3444c6d93fac\" /> | <img width=\"1000\" height=\"800\" alt=\"after-3\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/df585961-7830-45ca-9c1f-4c18717cae51\" /> |\r\n\r\nThe changes are separated into individual commits:\r\n- Preserve valid texels during dilation. (my original commit)\r\n- Correct grid traversal for nearly parallel rays.\r\n- Normalize interpolated bounce normals, which otherwise can shorten rays enough to stop before a wall.\r\n- Keep raster and bounce samples inside their triangles before applying bias.\r\n- Use geometric normals to reject opaque rays that point through the surface.\r\n- Keep shadow samples and their offsets on the visible side of geometry.\r\n- Correct the shadow sampling basis for downward light directions.\r\n- Remove the half-texel offset from rasterization and the corresponding seam-blending offsets.\r\n\r\nThe automated tests ran on macOS with an Apple M2 Pro using Metal. The complete patch removes the bright seams in the original 1k reproduction and the strong false glow in the updated smooth-mesh variants.\r\n\r\nAdditional sealed-room tests with flat and smooth normals produce exactly zero light, including the raw lighting data before denoising. The smooth room also passes with soft shadows and direct-light tracing at each bounce.\r\n\r\nThere are still limits: faint edge lines remain at 256-pixel resolution with the reproduction’s large bias of 0.05. That same bias produces a clean comparison at 1k. Vulkan, Direct3D, area lights, and transparent materials have not been validated, so this should be treated as an experimental patch rather than a complete fix for every lightmap artifact.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repo